Subject: [PATCH] SANE: accept requests for blocking I/O mode

SANE 1.05 section 4.3.12 requires support for blocking I/O.
The backend already operates in blocking mode, so acknowledge that
request while continuing to reject unsupported nonblocking mode.

--- a/src/SaneWrapper/backend.cpp
+++ b/src/SaneWrapper/backend.cpp
@@ -654,9 +654,8 @@
 sane_set_io_mode (SANE_Handle handle, SANE_Bool non_blocking)
 {
   SANE_TRACE_LOG("--------------sane_set_io_mode--------------");
- handle = handle;
- non_blocking = non_blocking;
- return SANE_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED;
+  (void) handle;
+  return non_blocking ? SANE_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED : SANE_STATUS_GOOD;
 }
 SANE_Status
 sane_get_select_fd (SANE_Handle handle, SANE_Int *fdp)
